tch": "Any late independent or nonpartisan polling, or movement in prediction markets, could tip the call either way in a race this close.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Jared Golden (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Maine's 2nd District is an open seat after Jared Golden's retirement, pairing state Auditor Matt Dunlap against two-time former governor Paul LePage. The district leans Republican by about four points, but recent polls from mid-September through mid-October show Dunlap ahead by two to six points, though most of that polling comes from Democratic sponsors. A nonpartisan UNH survey in September showed a six-point Dunlap lead.\n\nExpert raters are divided: Cook, Inside Elections, and Sabato's call it Lean R for a flip, while most others rate it a Tossup and FPO says Lean D. Prediction markets lean modestly toward LePage. Outside groups have spent heavily against both candidates. The race sits at a genuine tossup with a slight Democratic edge on recent polling, and ranked-choice voting could matter if minor candidates appear on the ballot.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.4239, "margin": -1.15}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.38, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.3812, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.377, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.3179, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.4062, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.4214, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.437, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.4556, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.4353, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.4338, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.4042, "margin": -2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.4713, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.3776, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.3456, "margin": -2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.3722, "ma